    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Shawn Shepherd",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "Cool little local spot to grab food and drinks where you can pull up in your boat (dock or right onto the sand).\nThere's a small beach and an extra bar area with live music.\n\nI am not a local (yet 😉) and felt a little overdressed arriving with a collared polo, khaki shorts and tennis shoes. So feel ",
        "time": "8 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Brent Ryals",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Great off the beaten path hangout. Mainly a boat up to place, we drove to it. The Bushwackers are great! So are the cheeseburgers. Can be busy at lunch. It's not classy, but a good atmosphere. Small beach for the kids to play on",
        "time": "4 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Phil R",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Second trip to Pirates Cove. Same as the first—still the same old waterfront dive bar that feels like it’s been frozen in time. If you’ve spent any time growing up around water with parents who just kind of let you roam free so they can drink in peace, you know exactly what I mean. Now that I’m an a",
        "time": "11 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Rick Koller",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "If you are into Dive bars this place is for you! We loved everything about this little place from the beach bar atmosphere to the open flame grilled burgers. Not to mention the tasty Drinks! We loved it so much we sent a group from our condo about 25-30 people to have a party! I did go there the wee",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Kerri Monroe-Stevens",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Haven’t eaten the food yet. Planning on it in near future, this is my newest treasure!! My pups ABSOLUTELY LOVE coming here, my little chihuahua loves to just roam and greet, while my other sweet blue heeler wants to play fetch! 🐾🥰💙",
        "time": "8 months ago"
      }
    ],
